"text":"2"}]}],"id":"blk-33212","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33214","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47525","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs verify-episode"},{"id":"spn-47526","text":" maps these directly (smoke-verified: tampered reward → 1, missing dir → 2, clean → 0). "},{"id":"spn-47527","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval-one --output"},{"id":"spn-47528","text":" now passes the wired verifier set into "},{"id":"spn-47529","marks":["code"],"text":"write_episode_bundle"},{"id":"spn-47530","text":", whose in-line staging verification exercises the exact closure a later "},{"id":"spn-47531","marks":["code"],"text":"verify-episode"},{"id":"spn-47532","text":" will."}]},{"id":"blk-33215","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-47533","text":"3. Corrected invariant (per your note)"}]},{"id":"blk-33216","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47534","text":"We no longer claim the whole episode directory is byte-identical across writes — the manifest carries a wall-clock "},{"id":"spn-47535","marks":["code"],"text":"created_at"},{"id":"spn-47536","text":". The correct invariant is: "},{"id":"spn-47537","marks":["bold"],"text":"the same evaluation → identical receipt → identical canonical evidence artifacts → the same episode id."},{"id":"spn-47538","text":" Pinned by "},{"id":"spn-47539","marks":["code"],"text":"test_fresh_independent_writes_share_canonical_artifacts"},{"id":"spn-47540","text":" (two independent roots share every canonical member; only "},{"id":"spn-47541","marks":["code"],"text":"created_at"},{"id":"spn-47542","text":" may differ)."}]},{"id":"blk-33217","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-47543","text":"4. Autonomous decisions flagged for your review"}]},{"id":"blk-33218","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33220","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47544","marks":["bold"],"text":"execution_facts reconstruction on replay"},{"id":"spn-47545","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-47546","marks":["code"],"text":"_reconstruct_execution_facts"},{"id":"spn-47547","text":"):"}]}],"id":"blk-33219","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-33221","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47548","text":"only "},{"id":"spn-47549","marks":["code"],"text":"agent_process"},{"id":"spn-47550","text":" (from the trace "},{"id":"spn-47551","marks":["code"],"text":"exit_code"},{"id":"spn-47552","text":" + manifest truncation flags) and "},{"id":"spn-47553","marks":["code"],"text":"sandbox"},{"id":"spn-47554","text":" (from the runner profile) are re-derivable from the bundle's own evidence; the irreducible run-time config (runner / platform / toolchain) is carried verbatim from the stored facts. A stored "},{"id":"spn-47555","marks":["code"],"text":"agent_process"},{"id":"spn-47556","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-47557","marks":["code"],"text":"sandbox"},{"id":"spn-47558","text":" that lies therefore moves the derived episode id and fails the receipt comparison."}]},{"id":"blk-33222","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33224","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47559","marks":["bold"],"text":"Sealed-implementation-driven replay wiring"},{"id":"spn-47560","text":" (step 5/11): the receipt's sealed"}]}],"id":"blk-33223","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-33225","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47561","text":"versions decide whether a scored signal is re-wired on replay. A demo that scores "},{"id":"spn-47562","marks":["code"],"text":"tests"},{"id":"spn-47563","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-47564","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-47565","text":" but left them unwired (sealed impl null) does NOT go "},{"id":"spn-47566","marks":["code"],"text":"unavailable"},{"id":"spn-47567","text":" when the CLI happens to wire them — it stays unwired to match what was sealed. Only a non-null sealed implementation demands a matching-version verifier."}]},{"id":"blk-33226","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33228","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47568","marks":["bold"],"text":"Idempotent reuse requires a full re-verify"},{"id":"spn-47569","text":" of the existing target (not just a"}]}],"id":"blk-33227","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-33229","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47570","text":"name/"},{"id":"spn-47571","marks":["code"],"text":"episode_id"},{"id":"spn-47572","text":" match), and a conflicting/corrupt target is a hard "},{"id":"spn-47573","marks":["code"],"text":"EpisodeBundleConflict"},{"id":"spn-47574","text":", never an overwrite."}]},{"id":"blk-33230","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47575","text":"Everything above is green with the real engine. No blocker — proceeding per the standing instruction. TestPlanV2 remains "},{"id":"spn-47576","marks":["bold"],"text":"not started"},{"id":"spn-47577","text":" as you directed."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaiera73rqjfah4loansfpd77fwlptedvgyqkhujkmil4fcd3wnd4chtua","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}